 "amendments_to_frozen_targets": [
  "A1: the definitions are wrapped in `noncomputable section` (attempts 02-03 failed with lean.dependsOnNoncomputable on koszul/riem/ricci/scal/reconGamma/reconC because of real division). Definition bodies and all target statements are unchanged.",
  "A2: helper theorems not listed in FROZEN_TARGETS.md were added: jacobiResidual_Cna_00..22 (nine slices of T3a, introduced after the monolithic 81-case proof hit the default 200000-heartbeat limit in attempts 02-03; no maxHeartbeats option is used), ricci_antisymm_01/_02/_12 (slices of T4b), reconGamma_eq (step of T9a). They are audited with the targets (39 theorems in total).",
  "A3: T4 `scal_Cna` keeps the card hypothesis `hna : n *ᵥ a = 0` but its proof does not use it (unused-variable linter warning); T4' records that the scalar contraction needs only n symmetric. n a = 0 is load-bearing exactly in T3a/T3b/T3d (Jacobi) and T4b/T4c (Ricci symmetry).",
  "A4: T7 `gamma_eq_DT_div` keeps `hij : i ≠ j` as the card states, though it is implied by the gap hypothesis (unused-variable linter warning)."
 ],
 "where_n_a_zero_is_used": {
  "jacobi": "jacobiResidual_Cna: residual = -2 eps_jkl (n a)_i, so Jacobi <-> n a = 0 (jacobi_iff_na_zero, bracket_jacobi)",
  "ricci": "ricci_antisymm_Cna: Ric_pq - Ric_qp = 2 eps_pqr (n a)_r, so Ricci symmetric <-> n a = 0",
  "scalar": "not used: scal_Cna_of_symm holds for symmetric n and arbitrary a",
  "symmetry_of_n": "load-bearing for the scalar formula: scal_nonsymm_control gives scal = -2 vs closed form 0 for a non-symmetric n with n a = 0"
 },
 "collision_branch": "DT_collision: lam_i = lam_j forces (D_k T)_ij = 0 for every metric-compatible Gamma; collision_witness: types I (C=0) and IX (n=1) with T = identity have identical DT but Gamma^2_01 = 0 vs 1/2, so the inverse formula does not apply. Python invariant_eigenframe_structure raises NumericalUnresolved on the same branch (numeric_crosscheck.json).",
 "bianchi_label_controls": "same_R3_I_VII0 (R3 = 0 for abelian I and non-abelian VII0), same_R3_IX_V (R3 = -6 for unimodular IX diag(1,1,6) and class-B V a=(1,0,0)), IX_R3_both_signs (IX gives R3 = 3/2 and -5/2). One R3 value does not fix a class; positive R3 is not claimed to imply IX.",
